{
  "id": "security-key-concepts-recap",
  "slug": "key-concepts-recap",
  "title": "Key Concepts Recap",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "definition",
      "heading": "Definition",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A Monolithic Application is a single-tiered software where all components are interconnected and run as one service."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 17,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "how-security-works",
      "heading": "How Security Works",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Authentication is handled when the client provides credentials (e.g., username/password).",
            "A session is created and stored (often server-side).",
            "The server checks the session and determines whether the user is authorized to access specific functionalities."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 34,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "example",
      "heading": "Example",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "User logs in → server stores session data → each request is checked using this session."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 16,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "definition",
      "heading": "Definition",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Microservices Architecture breaks the application into smaller, independent services that communicate via APIs."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 13,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "security-challenges",
      "heading": "Security Challenges",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Client only communicates with API Gateway (e.g., Zuul).",
            "Internal threats remain: Services behind the gateway cannot determine the origin of requests (user, service, or malicious actor).",
            "Unlike monoliths, there's no centralized session handling."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 33,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "heading": "Problem:",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Services cannot distinguish if a request came from:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Authenticated user",
            "Another microservice",
            "Malicious code/script"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 14,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1-secure-the-api-gateway-zuul",
      "heading": "Step 1: Secure the API Gateway (Zuul)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Dependency in infytel-zuul:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-security</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Annotations to Application Class:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@EnableOAuth2Sso   // Enables Single Sign-On using OAuth2\n@EnableZuulProxy   // Turns the app into a Zuul gateway",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Configuration in application.yml:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "yaml",
          "code": "client:\n  clientId: bd1c0a783ccdd1c9b9e4\n  clientSecret: 1a9030fbca47a5b2c28e92f19050bb77824b5ad1\n  accessTokenUri: https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token\n  userAuthorizationUri: https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize\n  clientAuthenticationScheme: form\nresource:\n  userInfoUri: https://api.github.com/user",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 13,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2-secure-each-microservice",
      "heading": "Step 2: Secure Each Microservice",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Dependency to Microservices:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-security</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Annotation in Application Class:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@EnableResourceServer   // Makes the service an OAuth2 resource server",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add Configuration in application.yml:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "yaml",
          "code": "client:\n  accessTokenUri: https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token\n  userAuthorizationUri: https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize\nresource:\n  userInfoUri: https://api.github.com/user",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 13,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "problem",
          "heading": "Problem",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "When a service (e.g., Product Service) calls another (e.g., Order Service), the OAuth token received from the gateway is not forwarded automatically."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 22,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "solution",
          "heading": "Solution",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Use a custom interceptor or RestTemplate configuration.",
                "Manually forward headers (esp. Authorization token)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 13,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();\nHttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();\nheaders.set(\"Authorization\", incomingRequest.getHeader(\"Authorization\"));\nHttpEntity<?> entity = new HttpEntity<>(headers);\nrestTemplate.exchange(\"http://orderservice/api/orders\", HttpMethod.GET, entity, String.class);",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "problem",
          "heading": "Problem",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Anyone can access the Config Server and retrieve sensitive properties from Git (e.g., DB credentials)."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 15,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "solution",
          "heading": "Solution",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                "Use Basic Authentication: ",
                "Encrypt Sensitive Data: "
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 6,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.cloud.config.server.encrypt.enabled=true",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Encrypt values using:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "bash",
              "code": "curl -u user:password http://localhost:8888/encrypt -d 'myDBpassword'",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Paste the encrypted value in the config file:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "yaml",
              "code": "spring:\n  datasource:\n    password: '{cipher}f3f2f1...encryptedText'",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
